<Page title={"Methodology"} description={"Editorial method: sources, the distinction between original analysis and external publications, corrections."} lang="en">
	<h1 class="page-title">Methodology</h1>
	<p class="page-lede">How this site produces and distinguishes its content.</p>
	<div class="page-body">
<h2>Two kinds of content</h2>
<p>The site clearly distinguishes:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Analysis</strong> — original pieces published here first.</li>
<li><strong>Publications</strong> — a portfolio of op-eds published in other outlets, with a canonical link to the source.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Sources</h2>
<p>Analyses rely on primary sources (official data, documents, interviews) that are cited and verifiable.</p>
<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>Any reported error is corrected transparently. See the Corrections page.</p>
	</div>
</Page>
